menu "Michi Music Stream WiFi"

    comment "Wi-Fi STA + BLE provisioning (phase 9). Credentials live ONLY in the NVS 'wifi' namespace - nothing here is a Wi-Fi credential."

    config MICHI_WIFI_RETRY_MAX
        int "Max reconnect attempts before RECOVERABLE_ERROR"
        default 3
        range 0 10
        help
          Consecutive STA disconnects tolerated before the FSM lands on
          RECOVERABLE_ERROR (MICHI_EVENT_ERROR is broadcast with
          ESP_ERR_WIFI_NOT_CONNECT as data; recovery via the physical
          button long press - MICHI_EVENT_RECOVER - or a reboot). 0 fails
          on the first disconnect.

    config MICHI_WIFI_RECONNECT_BASE_MS
        int "Reconnect backoff base (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 1000 60000
        help
          Backoff delay = BASE * 2^attempt, capped at 5 minutes, scheduled
          on a one-shot esp_timer (P0-11: never from the esp_event
          handler). With the defaults: 5 s, 10 s, 20 s, then
          RECOVERABLE_ERROR.

    config MICHI_PROV_POP
        string "BLE provisioning proof-of-possession (SRP6a)"
        default "michi123"
        help
          Proof-of-possession shown by the client (e.g. the Espressif
          Provisioning app) when starting the secure session. THIS IS A
          SHARED SECRET COMPILED INTO THE FIRMWARE: change it before any
          production deployment - a factory default PoP lets anyone on
          BLE range provision the device. It is a Kconfig STRING by
          design (the provisioning protocol needs it before the device is
          on the network); Wi-Fi credentials themselves are NEVER
          compiled in - they live only in NVS.

    config MICHI_PROV_SERVICE_NAME_PREFIX
        string "BLE provisioning service name prefix"
        default "MICHI-PROV_"
        help
          The provisioning BLE advertisement is
          <prefix><last 4 hex digits of the STA MAC> (e.g.
          MICHI-PROV_4CAB). Keep prefix + 4 characters within 31 bytes
          (BLE name limit); longer names are truncated by the BLE stack.

    config MICHI_PROV_RETRY_MS
        int "Automatic provisioning retry delay (ms)"
        default 30000
        range 5000 300000
        help
          After a failed provisioning session (10-min client timeout,
          bring-up error or NVS persist failure) the BLE provisioning
          service restarts automatically after this delay, max 3 retries.
          Exhausted sessions log clearly and land on UNPROVISIONED; the
          pairing button long press (recovery action) restarts the cycle.

    config MICHI_WIFI_TASK_STACK_BYTES
        int "Provisioning task stack (bytes)"
        default 6144
        range 4096 16384
        help
          Stack of the task that brings up the BLE provisioning service
          (wifi_prov_mgr + protocomm + cJSON device-info endpoint) and
          persists the delivered credentials. The BLE bring-up blocks
          this task, never the esp_event handlers (P0-11).

endmenu
